        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 136+ supports the HEVC/H265 codec in WebRTC; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5153479456456704\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5153479456456704</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds details of this to <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Media/Guides/Formats/WebRTC_codecs\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Media/Guides/Formats/WebRTC_codecs</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I searched around MDN, but didn't really see anywhere else where I should mention this.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
